Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||05-20-2001||01:14 AM||||I found what is really wrong with my car. When I bought it I noticed mice turds on the top of the engine, and asked the previous owner if the 'pets' were extra $$$ ? <P>  didnt think about that since. I have been debugging my engine problems for the last week or so, and decided to trace out the few vacuum lines that dissapear under the intake plenium.<P>  I followed the one from the map sensor (my code 33) under the air intake plenium and had to cram my head back into the engine to see where it went, and - what the heck?! that cant be right! there was a notch in the short rubber tube that attaches it to the pressure regulator.<P>  I could just barely reach one finger under there where it goes to the fuel pressure regulator, and sure enough, there was a hole chewed in the side of the rubber hose under there!<P>  I pulled the intake plenium and could not stop laughing. You can see the teeth marks onthe thing, and the hole in the side is as big as the inside of the tube! Creature Damage!<P>  Thats one you dont see in the shop manuals - code 33: look for vacuum lines chewed up by mice!<P>  I also noticed the ERG metal line is cracked right at the intake plenium, so I have two major vacuum leaks here that Im fixing together.<P>  I excited and looking forward to getting the gaskets and the EGR tube and painting the plenium and putting this baby back together.  I thought I might of had a stuck injector, but according to the service manual a vacuum leak on the MAP senosor accounts for all the problems I have been seeing.<P>  does the forum give out awards for most unsual problem solved - Creature damage has to be a new catigory!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||05-20-2001||09:36 AM||||BTW, my son was looking at all the plumbing in the engine compartment and said, "wow this car has a lot of vacuum tubes in it!"<P>I stopped and put my hands on my hips and said indignatly,"this car does NOT have ANY vacuum tubes in it! It has an onboard computer and its 100% SOLID STATE!"||||reg||1
